Given, \[A=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; 0\\
0 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]\] \[B=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
0\\
1
\end{array}\right]\] \[C=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 2
\end{array}\right]\] To check controllability, form the controllability matrix, \[Q_{c}
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
B &amp; AB
\end{array}\right]\] First compute \(AB\), \[AB=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; 0\\
0 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
0\\
1
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
0\\
-2
\end{array}\right]\] Therefore, \[Q_{c}
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0 &amp; 0\\
1 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]\] \[|Q_{c}|=0\] Hence, controllability matrix does not have full rank. Therefore, the system is not completely controllable. Hence,Statement B is true Now check observability. Observability matrix is, \[Q_{o}
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
C\\
CA
\end{array}\right]\] First compute \(CA\), \[CA=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 2
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; 0\\
0 &amp; -2
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; -4
\end{array}\right]\] Therefore, \[Q_{o}
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 2\\
-1 &amp; -4
\end{array}\right]\] \[|Q_{o}|=-4+2=-2\neq0\] Hence, observability matrix has full rank. Therefore, the system is completely observable. Hence, Statement C is true Therefore, correct options are B and C. \[\boxed{
\text{(B) The system is not completely controllable} 
}\] \[\boxed{
\text{(C) The system is completely observable}}\]

